Below is a **Graphviz DOT script** for a colourful, dark-themed schematic of **k‑fold cross‑validation for hyperparameter tuning**. It shows three phases: preparation, the k‑fold loop (one detailed fold + “repeat” placeholder), and result selection.

### How to render it

Save the code as `kfolding_cv.dot` and run:

```bash
# Install Graphviz if needed
sudo apt-get install graphviz        # Linux
brew install graphviz                  # macOS

# Render PNG
dot -Tpng -o kfolding_cv.png kfolding_cv.dot

# Or render SVG
dot -Tsvg -o kfolding_cv.svg kfolding_cv.dot
```

---

### Full DOT code

```dot
digraph KFoldHyperTune {
  rankdir=TB;
  bgcolor="#0B1D3A";                      // deep navy background
  fontname="sans-serif";
  fontsize=12;
  label="K-Fold Cross-Validation for Hyperparameter Tuning";
  labelloc=r;
  labeljust=l;
  margins=0.5;
  pad=0.4;
  splines=ortho;
  class [fontsize=9, edgecolor="#A8C8E0"];

  // ==================== Phase 1: Preparation ====================
  subgraph cluster_prep {
    label="1. Data - Search Space - Controller";
    style=invis;
    clustercolor="#2C3E50";
    padding=12;

    Dataset [
      shape=ellipse,
      fillcolor="#4A90D9",
      strokecolor="#BDD7EE",
      fontcolor="#FFFFFF",
      style=filled,
      penwidth=2,
      width=1.8,
      height=1.0,
      label="Dataset\n(D, X, Y)";
    ];

    HyperSpace [
      shape=box,
      fillcolor="#5B8DEF",
      strokecolor="#AED6F1",
      fontcolor="#FFFFFF",
      style=filled,
      penwidth=1.8,
      width=2.2,
      height=0.8,
      label="Hyperparameter Space\n(model, lr, dropout, patience...)";
    ];

    KFoldCtrl [
      shape=box,
      fillcolor="#3CA0B2",
      strokecolor="#7FD8E8",
      fontcolor="#FFFFFF",
      style=filled,
      penwidth=1.8,
      width=1.8,
      height=0.8,
      label="K-Fold Controller\nk = 5, 10, ...";
    ];

    Dataset --> HyperSpace;
    HyperSpace --> KFoldCtrl;
  }

  // ==================== Phase 2: K-Fold Loop ====================
  subgraph cluster_cv {
    label="2. K-Fold Cross-Validation";
    style=invis;
    clustercolor="#8E44AD";
    padding=14;

    KFods [
      shape=shell,
      fillcolor="#9B59B6",
      strokecolor="#D9B3EF",
      fontcolor="#FFFFFF",
      style=filled,
      penwidth=2,
      width=2.6,
      height=1.2,
      label="K-Fold Tuning Loop\nFor i = 1 to k";
    ];

    KFoldCtrl --> KFods;

    // ---- Detailed example: Fold 1 ----
    subgraph cluster_fold1_exp {
      label="Fold 1 - Expanded Pattern";
      style=invis;
      clustercolor="#E67E22";
      padding=8;

      ExpTrain [
        shape=cylinder,
        fillcolor="#3498DB",
        strokecolor="#A8DFF0",
        fontcolor="#FFFFFF",
        style=filled,
        penwidth=1.4,
        width=1.6,
        height=0.9,
        label="Train Set";
      ];

      ExpTest [
        shape=circle,
        fillcolor="#E74C3C",
        strokecolor="#FAB8C2",
        fontcolor="#FFFFFF",
        style=filled,
        penwidth=1.4,
        diameter=1.1,
        label="Test Set";
      ];

      ExpTrainer [
        shape=prism6,
        fillcolor="#1ABC9C",
        strokecolor="#5BE1D1",
        fontcolor="#FFFFFF",
        style=filled,
        penwidth=1.4,
        width=1.8,
        height=0.9,
        label="Train/Validate";
      ];

      ExpModel [
        shape=hexagon,
        fillcolor="#6C5CE7",
        strokecolor="#A29BFE",
        fontcolor="#FFFFFF",
        style=filled,
        penwidth=1.4,
        width=1.6,
        height=0.9,
        label="Model";
      ];

      EvalExp [
        shape=box,
        fillcolor="#FDCB6E",
        strokecolor="#FFEAA7",
        fontcolor="#7D6608",
        style=filled,
        penwidth=1.4,
        width=1.8,
        height=0.6,
        label="Evaluate\n(metric)";
      ];

      ScoreExp [
        shape=note,
        fillcolor="#FBFCDF",
        strokecolor="#D9D9D9",
        fontcolor="#444444",
        style=filled,
        penwidth=1.2,
        width=1.6,
        height=0.7,
        label="Fold Score";
      ];

      AccExp [
        shape=box,
        fillcolor="#BDC3C7",
        strokecolor="#EBEDED",
        fontcolor="#2C3E50",
        style=filled,
        penwidth=1.4,
        width=1.5,
        height=0.7,
        label="Accumulate this fold";
      ];

      ExpTrain --> ExpTrainer;
      ExpTrainer --> ExpModel;
      ExpModel --> EvalExp;
      ExpTest --> EvalExp;
      EvalExp --> ScoreExp;
      ScoreExp --> AccExp;
      ExpTrain -- ExpTest [
        style=dashed,
        color="#EAEAEA",
        label="data split";
      ];
    }

    // ---- Remaining folds (same pattern) ----
    subgraph cluster_remaining_folds {
      label="Folds 2..k - Same Pattern";
      style=invis;
      clustercolor="#E67E22";

      RemFold [
        shape=cloud,
        fillcolor="#F1C40F",
        strokecolor="#F39C12",
        fontcolor="#7D6608",
        style=filled,
        penwidth=1.6,
        width=2.4,
        height=1.3,
        label="Repeated for k-1:\ntrain/validate/\nmodel/evaluate";
      ];

      AccExp --> AGG;
      RemFold --> AGG;
    }

    AGG [
      shape=box,
      fillcolor="#2C3E50",
      strokecolor="#7F8C8D",
      fontcolor="#FFFFFF",
      style=filled,
      penwidth=1.8,
      width=1.8,
      height=0.8,
      label="Aggregate Scores\nMean +/- Std";
    ];
  }

  // ==================== Phase 3: Result ====================
  subgraph cluster_result {
    label="3. Best Hyperparameters & Report";
    style=invis;
    clustercolor="#27AE60";
    padding=14;

    FINAL [
      shape=diamond,
      fillcolor="#E170E5",
      strokecolor="#AD1457",
      fontcolor="#FFFFFF",
      style=filled,
      penwidth=2,
      width=2.2,
      height=1.3,
      label="Best Hyperparameters\nAvg Performance";
    ];

    REPORT [
      shape=note,
      fillcolor="#9B59B6",
      strokecolor="#E4AEC4",
      fontcolor="#FFFFFF",
      style=filled,
      penwidth=1.6,
      width=2.6,
      height=1.2,
      label="Performance Report\nIntervals, plots";
    ];

    SELECTED [
      shape=box,
      fillcolor="#27AE60",
      strokecolor="#A5F3C8",
      fontcolor="#FFFFFF",
      style=filled,
      penwidth=1.8,
      width=2.4,
      height=0.8,
      label="Selected Configurations\nfor deployment";
    ];

    AGG --> FINAL;
    FINAL --> SELECTED;
    FINAL --> REPORT;
  }
}
```

---

### What the diagram shows

1. **Preparation** – dataset, hyperparameter space, and a k‑fold controller.
2. **K‑fold loop** – for each fold:
   - Split data into **Train** and **Test**.
   - **Train** a model on the train set.
   - **Evaluate** on the test set.
   - Record a **fold score** and **accumulate** it.
   - The last `k-1` folds follow the same pattern (shown as a gold cloud placeholder).
3. **Results** – aggregate scores, select the best hyperparameters, and generate a performance report.

You can change `k` by editing the `Folds 2..k` placeholder or adding more identical fold blocks. The colours are deliberately grouped by phase for easy reading.

