Assistant B is simpler and includes `autoplay`, `muted`, and `playsinline`, so it is more likely to deliver the requested background video behavior. However, its button starts with fully white text and an outline rather than appearing faded out as requested. Its video positioning could also be made more robust by using fixed positioning and explicit viewport dimensions.

Overall, B’s straightforward implementation avoids A’s broken extra script and handles video autoplay better. A matches the faded-button detail more closely, but its functional issues outweigh that advantage. [[B>A]]
